@@ -24,6 +24,16 @@ The original barriers and alias rules remain in force. CPU Vulkan checks cover
 production ShadowCopy dispatch, access stages, padding and independent writes;
 A840 frame performance requires a hardware capture.
 
+Internal transfer buffers use Vulkan's preferred copy offset and row alignment.
+The conversion kernel carries the actual transfer pitch, while Metal-visible
+heap offsets, padding and alias contents retain their layout. This lets Turnip
+record a two-dimensional image copy instead of splitting unaligned rows into
+individual blits. Vulkan operation records retain the recording thread identity
+for correlation with encoder timings. Image-to-buffer records also carry the
+region count; a single-region record includes its buffer row length and the
+low 32 bits of its buffer offset, so row and offset alignment can be checked.
+These timestamps are CPU recording boundaries, not GPU copy durations.
+
 ## Frame diagnostics
 
 The iPhone24A446 build profile excludes iPad-specific image-relative QuartzCore
